selLab('l-win','Windows','Windows event-log investigation','Reconstruct an intrusion from Security log events.',`<p>Event extract from a Windows server. Answer each question.</p><div class='term' style='height:auto'>09:01:12 4625 Failed logon jsmith src 10.0.0.77 (x8)\n09:01:40 4624 Logon success jsmith src 10.0.0.77 type 10\n09:03:05 4688 cmd.exe /c whoami /all by jsmith\n09:04:20 4720 Account created: helpdesk2 by jsmith\n09:04:31 4732 helpdesk2 added to Administrators\n09:06:50 7045 Service installed: UpdSvc (C:/Users/Public/upd.exe)\n09:12:09 1102 Audit log cleared by jsmith</div>`,[['Events 4625 then 4624 suggest...','Password guessing, then a successful login',['Normal password reset','Password guessing, then a successful login','Disk failure']],['Logon type 10 means...','Remote interactive logon (RDP)',['Local keyboard logon','Service logon','Remote interactive logon (RDP)']],['Which events show persistence?','4720 account creation and 7045 service install',['4625 only','4688 only','4720 account creation and 7045 service install']],['What happened at 09:12?','The attacker cleared the audit log to hide tracks',['A routine log rotation','The attacker cleared the audit log to hide tracks','A backup finished']],['Best first response?','Disable jsmith, remove helpdesk2 and UpdSvc, isolate the host, preserve logs',['Reboot the server','Delete the log','Disable jsmith, remove helpdesk2 and UpdSvc, isolate the host, preserve logs']]],'Investigation complete: brute force, RDP access, privilege creation, persistence and anti-forensics.');
selLab('l-fw','Network','Firewall rule exercise','Apply default deny and least privilege to a network.',`<p>Web server 192.0.2.10 sits in a DMZ. Database 10.0.1.5 is internal. Admin workstation is 10.0.0.5. Policy: <b>default deny</b>, allow only what is required.</p>`,[['Internet to web server, TCP 443',AD[0],AD],['Internet to web server, TCP 22 (SSH)',AD[1],AD],['Admin 10.0.0.5 to web server, TCP 22',AD[0],AD],['Internet to database, TCP 3306',AD[1],AD],['Web server to database, TCP 3306',AD[0],AD],['Any other traffic not listed (default rule)',AD[1],AD]],'Rule set correct: only required flows are allowed and everything else is denied.');
